// `@doc { … }` brace escapes (text-tiers arc): `\{` and `\}` are literal braces the balance scan
// does not count, and `\\` is a literal backslash — so prose can hold *unbalanced* braces. Every
// other backslash is ordinary text (markdown keeps its own escapes). The body below closes only
// at the final unescaped `}`; the program still runs clean.
// expect: stdout "ok"
// expect: exit 0
@doc {
  A lone closer \} and a lone opener \{ are fine; so is a trailing backslash \\
  and markdown's own \*escape\* (the backslashes before `*` pass through).
}

echo "ok"
